A. leg

The class dad / dab / gut / low / cat is a plain C V C class with a medial vowel in {a,u,o} and a closing consonant in {b,d,t,w}, and it is built from the inventory {a,b,c,d,g,l,o,t,u,w}.  That is the same as C V C and {e,m,p,r}-free, because e,m,p,r are exactly the letters that are systematically absent from the five positives and systematically present in the five negatives

ear e,r ; cop p ; ego e ; mom m ; ate e

* leg = l e g is C V C but it brings in the forbidden medial e. e never occurs as a medial vowel in dad dab gut low cat and e is the vowel that marks ear/ego/ate as negatives;

dam brings in the forbidden m, the m-analogue of mom, and final m ∉ {b,d,t,w};
rat and car bring in the forbidden r that marks ear as a negative;
bin is e,m,p,r-free but has medial i ∉ {a,u,o} and final n ∉ {b,d,t,w}.

Hence leg is the canonical, least controversial counter-example to the dad/dab/gut/low/cat class: it keeps the C V C shape but violates the e-free vowel/inventory that defines the class.

